# Everything the image must never contain.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter: `.env` holds live credentials
# and `data/` holds somebody's research. A container image is copied, pushed to
# a registry and pulled by machines you do not control — neither belongs in one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/

node_modules
client/dist
dist

.git
.gitignore
tests
docs
*.md
!README.md

# The inputs the deployed Brain reads by path, re-included explicitly.
#
# `blueprints/` is not excluded by anything above — and saying so out loud is
# the point. `*.md` is a single-segment pattern, so by Docker's own matching it
# covers markdown at the *root* of the context and not inside a directory; the
# blueprint is `blueprints/Brain_Intelligence_Map.md` and is therefore safe. That
# is a fact about BuildKit's semantics rather than about this repository, it
# cannot be tested without a daemon, and the cost of being wrong about it is a
# failed deploy — which this directory has already caused once, when it lived
# under `docs/` and the build answered `"/docs/capability": not found`.
#
# So the exception is written down rather than reasoned about. It is a no-op if
# the semantics are what I believe, and it is the fix if they are not.
!blueprints
!blueprints/**

# Build and editor noise.
.vscode
.idea
*.log
coverage
.DS_Store
